-- SnapshotsMy.HashContainers: the module as a Program of the one grammar of `LeanScript.Expr`.
-- 🎯 a public entry point of the module; 📦 a declaration the translation pulled in.
-- Every term below is a `Term`, so it is terminating by construction.  A recursion is
-- one of the four schemes of `LeanScript.FixSplit` — `fixStructTail`, `fixStructDeep`,
-- `fixWfTail`, `fixWfDeep` — the product of *how it descends* (structurally, on one
-- named argument, in the order the language fixes; or well-foundedly, on the subject
-- Lean's `termination_by` names) by *where the self call stands* (tail: a `while`
-- loop, no frame; deep: native recursion).  No scheme carries a measure the front end
-- had to invent.  A `Tail` scheme's `by decide` is the check that every self call is
-- in tail position; the descent field is Lean's own `decreasing_by` proof, and it is
-- rendered as `sorry` because the front end does not transcribe proof terms yet.
-- What became of the declarations of the module:
--   2 are programs below
--   1 is refused by the totality gate
--   5 have no type in the grammar, and can have none
--   3 are gaps the front end would have to grow to cover (`TERM_REMAINING_REFUSALS.md`)
-- Every declaration with no program of its own is a line below, with the reason it has none.
-- no type of the grammar describes it, and none can: `List.forIn'.loop._at_.test1.spec_2`: the parameter `m` of `Std.DHashMap.Internal.Raw₀.Const.getD._at_.test1.spec_0` has type `Subtype
--   lcErased`, which the front end does not translate — part of it was erased by the compiler to `lcAny`, which is what happens to a value whose type is not known statically — the state of an existential type, say — and no `Ty` denotes such a value
-- no type of the grammar describes it, and none can: `List.forIn'.loop._at_.test4.spec_0`: the parameter `β` of `Std.DHashMap.Internal.Raw₀.insert._at_.test1.spec_1` has type `String →
--   Type`, which the front end does not translate — it answers with a `Sort`, so it is a type constructor or the motive of a dependent eliminator rather than a type of values, and the front end has no higher-kinded types
-- outside the fragment: `List.mapTR.loop._at_.test6.spec_0`: `List.reverse` is polymorphic, and the call says nothing about what type it is called at; the front end translates one instantiation at a time
-- refused by the totality gate: `_private.Init.Data.Array.Basic.0.Array.foldrMUnsafe.fold._at_.test6.spec_2`: it is a specialisation of `_private.Init.Data.Array.Basic.0.Array.foldrMUnsafe.fold`, which is an `unsafe def`, so Lean did not prove it terminating; the backend cannot turn it into a loop
-- left out with what it calls: `test1`: it calls `List.forIn'.loop._at_.test1.spec_2`, whose own line above says why that one has no program
-- no type of the grammar describes it, and none can: `test2`: the parameter `m` of `Std.DHashMap.Internal.Raw₀.Const.get?._at_.test2.spec_2` has type `Subtype
--   lcErased`, which the front end does not translate — part of it was erased by the compiler to `lcAny`, which is what happens to a value whose type is not known statically — the state of an existential type, say — and no `Ty` denotes such a value
-- outside the fragment: `test3`: `Std.DHashMap.Internal.AssocList.nil` builds a value of `Std.DHashMap.Internal.AssocList String fun x =>
--   PUnit`, and the front end has no `Ty` for that type — `PUnit` has one value, which carries no information: such a type is erased before a `Ty` is built, and the front end does not drop a field of one yet
-- outside the fragment: `test4`: `Std.DHashMap.Internal.AssocList.nil` builds a value of `Std.DHashMap.Internal.AssocList String fun x =>
--   PUnit`, and the front end has no `Ty` for that type — `PUnit` has one value, which carries no information: such a type is erased before a `Ty` is built, and the front end does not drop a field of one yet
-- no type of the grammar describes it, and none can: `test5`: the parameter `β` of `Std.DHashMap.Internal.Raw₀.erase._at_.test5.spec_0` has type `String →
--   Type`, which the front end does not translate — it answers with a `Sort`, so it is a type constructor or the motive of a dependent eliminator rather than a type of values, and the front end has no higher-kinded types
-- left out with what it calls: `test6`: it calls `List.forIn'.loop._at_.test4.spec_0`, whose own line above says why that one has no program
-- no type of the grammar describes it, and none can: `test7`: the parameter `m` of `Std.DHashMap.Internal.Raw₀.Const.getD._at_.test1.spec_0` has type `Subtype
--   lcErased`, which the front end does not translate — part of it was erased by the compiler to `lcAny`, which is what happens to a value whose type is not known statically — the state of an existential type, say — and no `Ty` denotes such a value
